# Imperial Backend Architecture

## Overview
The Imperial backend is a Node.js/TypeScript application using Express.js with a modular, feature-based architecture. It implements AI-powered chat functionality with UI generation capabilities using LangGraph.

## Core Technologies
- **Runtime**: Node.js with TypeScript
- **Framework**: Express.js
- **Database**: SQLite with Drizzle ORM
- **AI**: LangChain/LangGraph for chat workflows
- **Authentication**: JWT with refresh token rotation
- **Testing**: Jest with Supertest
- **Build**: TypeScript compiler with tsconfig

## Folder Structure

```
backend/src/
├── @types/                    # Global type definitions
│   └── error.types.ts        # Error definition interfaces
├── config/                   # Application configuration
│   └── constants.ts          # App-wide constants and configs
├── core/                     # Core utilities and shared logic
│   └── utils/
│       └── responseFormatter.ts # Standardized error handling
├── feat/                     # Feature modules (main business logic)
│   ├── auth/                 # Authentication & authorization
│   ├── chat/                 # AI chat and UI generation
│   ├── library/              # Component library management
│   ├── rag/                  # Retrieval Augmented Generation
│   └── vectorStore/          # Vector storage services
├── shared/                   # Shared utilities across features
│   └── repository/           # Common repository patterns
├── services/                 # External service integrations
│   ├── llm/                  # Language model services
│   └── rag/                  # RAG service implementations
├── test-utils/               # Testing utilities and setup
├── db.ts                     # Database connection setup
├── env.ts                    # Environment variable validation
├── schema.ts                 # Database schema definitions
└── server.ts                 # Application entry point
```

## Key Architectural Patterns

### 1. Feature-Based Organization
Each feature in `feat/` follows a consistent structure:
- **Controllers**: Handle HTTP requests/responses
- **Services**: Business logic implementation
- **Routes**: Express route definitions
- **Validation**: Request/response validation schemas
- **Repositories**: Data access layer
- **Types**: Feature-specific type definitions

### 2. Modular Chat Architecture
The chat feature uses a sophisticated LangGraph-based workflow:
- **Graph Nodes**: Modular processing units (`nodes/` directory)
- **Shared Services**: Common utilities for LLM and vector operations
- **State Management**: Centralized graph state with checkpointing
- **Real-time Updates**: SSE (Server-Sent Events) for progress streaming

### 3. Error Handling
Standardized error handling using:
- Custom `AppError` class extending native Error
- Structured error definitions with HTTP status codes
- Global error middleware for consistent responses
- Validation error formatting with field-specific details

### 4. Database Patterns
- **ORM**: Drizzle ORM with SQLite
- **Migrations**: Version-controlled schema changes
- **Type Safety**: Full TypeScript integration
- **Testing**: Isolated test database with migration support

## Entry Points
- **Development**: `yarn dev` (nodemon with TypeScript)
- **Production**: `yarn start` (compiled JavaScript)
- **Testing**: `yarn test` (Jest with coverage)
- **Database**: `yarn migrate` (run migrations)

## Configuration Files
- [package.json](mdc:backend/package.json) - Dependencies and scripts
- [tsconfig.json](mdc:backend/tsconfig.json) - TypeScript configuration
